<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Lever Bros rises 1.60 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Lever Bros rises 1.60 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lever Brothers Pakistan Ltd shares  rose 15 rupees, or 1.60 percent, to 955 on Friday on buying by foreign  investors ahead of an earnings announcement, dealers at the Karachi  Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The company will announce results for the year ended June 30 in a  few weeks.</p>
<p>Some 440 shares changed hands in two hours of trading at 11.30 a.m.  (0630 GMT), one dealer said.</p>
<p>The company manufactures consumer items including edible oils and  tea.</p>
<p>The company paid a 100 percent cash dividend for the 18 months ended  June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
